{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Aerith","id":"260949833773219840","is_bot":0,"username":"aerith_of_aer"},"author_id":"260949833773219840","channel_id":"736448287510495254","content":"From the top left part of the pinky finger. Down to the base of the thumb. He makes a line that crosses through the other four. \"Navar.\" He says the name quietly","created_at":"2020-07-31T13:27:53.473000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"738749782574497885","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Aerith","id":"260949833773219840","is_bot":0,"username":"aerith_of_aer"},"author_id":"260949833773219840","channel_id":"736448287510495254","content":"He wraps his bloody mess of a paw in bandages. He tries his best to not show the pain but it is all there. Not just the physical, but the emotional of knowing he could have talked Navar down. He had the ability, and didn't. And For what? \n\nHope\n\nThe hope that he would return smiling like he never had before. That old tired face would show the signs of happiness once more. That they could share a drink together and laugh.\n\nThe truth is Navar didn't need to go to make all those things happen. If Cato had been a better friend.","created_at":"2020-07-31T13:32:17.899000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"738750891657789551","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
